false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000177614","entrez_id":["79605"],"uniprot":["Q8N414"],"ncbi_summary":"The piggyBac family of proteins, found in diverse animals, are transposases related to the transposase of the canonical piggyBac transposon from the moth, Trichoplusia ni. This family also includes genes in several genomes, including human, that appear to have been derived from the piggyBac transposons. This gene belongs to the subfamily of piggyBac transposable element derived (PGBD) genes. The PGBD proteins appear to be novel, with no obvious relationship to other transposases, or other known protein families. [provided by RefSeq, May 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q8N414","text":"Transposase that mediates sequence-specific genomic rearrangements (PubMed:26406119, PubMed:28504702). Can induce genomic rearrangements that inactivate the HPRT1 gene (PubMed:27491780)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}